{"kind":"report","text":"Hugh has reviewed these findings in chat and now explicitly asks: \"please send this feedback to the primary planner instance and request they task appropriately.\" Please reconcile this with existing owned work, then assign bounded implementation and acceptance follow-ups appropriately. Report the resulting ownership, sequence, acceptance criteria and any product decisions that still require Hugh. Do not duplicate already commissioned work.\n\nRead-only design comparison at main 38b0b2f2b: all six Sprint 14 captures, retained mobile/creation/local-label captures, current Page/CLI source and accepted Plan 027 v2 design. The visual shell has improved substantially: rail, typography, spacing and a single detail status follow the design. Design conformance remains incomplete in these significant respects:\n\n1. Highest priority: primary actions still resemble a debugger's form catalogue. Create issue is a collapsed section below Inspect room record in notes/2026-10-09-demo-captures/room.png. Comment, Review and Merge follow the same pattern. packages/page/src/actions.ts:63-74 renders every primary action as a disclosure; main.ts:421/430 places actions after the subject screen and its record inspection. Required technical fields remain ordinary inputs (actions.ts:119); merge requires report fact references (packages/lanes/src/change.ts:1283). Steering: creation in the list toolbar, comment composer with the conversation, one prominent next action per change, and consolidated record inspection in a secondary menu. Preserve native typed signing and authority while implementing actual task forms.\n\n2. Ordinary page editing and path correction are missing. The invalid-path screenshot says \"Choose a file path inside this room\" but offers no Fix path control (packages/page/src/view.ts:110-118). Pages navigates directly to the site (main.ts:130). Advanced propose-file requires base, digest, size and content (packages/lanes/src/change.ts:829-837), with no task-specific defaults for it (main.ts:414-418). Steering: agree the supported editing journey, provide task-specific controls that derive technical values from selected content, and respect native limits on replacing/correcting an existing proposal. Do not invent an unsupported in-place correction.\n\n3. Reviewing changes and opening results remain short of the selected-version design. The accepted v2 change screen shows a diff and opens the selected merged page. Current view.ts:112 offers literal source in a disclosure, tree proposals have no file preview, and Open latest page points at HEAD (data.ts:473). These are explicitly accepted interim limits in notes/2026-10-09-page-v2-delivery.md:25-29, not dishonest preview labels. Keep authenticated base-to-proposal diff and immutable page opening as completion criteria under existing owners. Extend the design through published reading: site-page.png and packages/scope/src/site/route.ts:252-256 still foreground repository/branch/commit chrome and \"The room's page\".\n\n4. Original easy-path initialization remains open. Browser creation requires an existing room/member context and configured founding eligibility (main.ts:388-398); a fresh browser sees invitation/config/key settings (main.ts:265-275). CLI easy-path 027.2 remains proposed/uncommissioned (plans/027-artroom-usability/handoffs/027-02-easy-path-cli.md:5). CLI global context and native claiming do not provide an application preset. Main line.ts:60 has no propose dispatch; Sprint 14:73-84 says the branch workflow is unlanded with gate/hosted/review duties outstanding. Steering: define first-use acceptance as a person reaching an application-ready room from an empty folder/browser, separately from native scope creation. Coordinate with 006/025/027 owners and the current manifest delivery; do not create a competing manifest gate or enlarge it into generic recovery.\n\n5. Room identity/switching needs a product decision. \"Room name\" is a browser-local label alongside the generated repository name (label/local-label-light-320.png; main.ts:121-125). The apparent room switcher opens Settings, not the designed room picker. Local naming was explicitly accepted in delivery.md:37-41; this is an accepted narrowing whose product implications remain. Determine whether friendly identity is shared or personal, use accurate wording and provide direct room selection when supported.\n\n6. List navigation loses working context. view.ts:37-38 reconstructs Open plus empty search; back links at :24 and routeOf in shell.ts:18-24 do not preserve query/filter. Opening a searched or closed item and returning requires finding it again. Steering: preserve room-specific query/filter through detail navigation and refresh. Small, high-value correction.\n\nContinue existing required follow-ups without duplicates: clear only a successfully posted comment draft while preserving newer/unsent/refused/unknown edits (delivery.md:177-180); retain uncertain generic/enrollment submissions across reload and provide usable recovery rather than protocol inspection (delivery.md:20-23,147-155).\n\nAcceptance: Sprint screenshots are recorded presentation at earlier source efb5c56d, not completed hosted acceptance of landed source. Capture README and Sprint 14:41-55 explicitly preserve that limit. Reconcile the started Page v2 rehearsal; verify current end-to-end journey plus physical phone/virtual keyboard, zoom and assistive technology before claiming no-compromise usability. Existing gate remains recorded; this review changed no source and ran no repeated gate.\n\nRecommended prioritization: action hierarchy, editing/review journey, first-use creation, then room identity; retain the small list/draft corrections as bounded work. Product decisions and dependency ownership should be explicit; source approval alone does not establish design acceptance.\n\nNo source changes or new implementation tasks were published by this review before Hugh authorized this handoff. The initial review-tracking entry had been initiated before his temporary instruction to keep proposed tasks in chat.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","requested_action":"Primary planner: reconcile, prioritize and task the discussed design deviations appropriately, retaining existing owners and explicit acceptance criteria."}}